    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "net: prevent ASMap group collisions and honor map filenames",
    "user": {
      "login": "l0rinc",
      "id": 1841944,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDE5NDQ=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1841944?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/l0rinc",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "**Problem:** A mapped autonomous system and an unmapped IPv6 /32 can share an address group, so the node treats unrelated peers as part of the same network when selecting connections.\nA node started with `-asmap=2026-09-asmap.dat` can also silently select the embedded map.\n\n**Fix:** Give mapped autonomous systems their own group tag. Nodes using ASMap rebucket stored peers once on upgrade or downgrade across this change.\n\n- Load digit-leading filenames from disk. `-asmap`, `-asmap=` and `-asmap=1` still select the embedded map. `-asmap=2` now names a file.\n- Report failed path lookups as missing files, and directories or read failures as invalid maps.\n- Require a new destination for `exportasmap`. A repeated export is cheap to regenerate, but exporting over a custom map silently changes what the node loads on restart. Callers reusing a path must first move or remove the file. [Original overwrite rationale](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/33920#discussion_r3117087307)\n- Fix the `decode --nonoverlapping` documentation and help text, and describe how `diff_addrs` groups peers by their old and new AS assignments.\n\n---\n\nI batched these fixes because I don't have the bandwidth to maintain several ASMap PRs. Feel free to carve out and merge individual commits. The [ASMap optimizations](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36994) can be merged independently.\n",
